From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SQ2 Mesa fork
Subject: [PATCH] d3d12: silence C4189 on bUsedAsReference in codec-less builds

Build-compat only, no behavior change. With -Dvideo-codecs= (empty)
every VIDEO_CODEC_*ENC is 0, so all switch branches that pass
bUsedAsReference compile out and newer MSVC (VS18, cl 14.52) fires
C4189, which Mesa promotes via /we4189 AFTER any user -Dcpp_args
suppression -- so no flag ordering can silence it. Mark the variable
[[maybe_unused]], matching existing precedent in this file
(last_slice_completion_fence). mmozeiko's older MSVC never emitted
the warning here, which is why his build.cmd needs no equivalent.

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_video_enc.cpp b/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_video_enc.cpp
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_video_enc.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_video_enc.cpp
@@ -763,7 +763,7 @@ d3d12_video_encoder_update_picparams_tracking
       d3d12_video_encoder_get_current_picture_param_settings_mutable(pD3D12Enc);

    enum pipe_video_format codec = u_reduce_video_profile(pD3D12Enc->base.profile);
-   bool bUsedAsReference = false;
+   [[maybe_unused]] bool bUsedAsReference = false;
    switch (codec) {
 #if VIDEO_CODEC_H264ENC
       case PIPE_VIDEO_FORMAT_MPEG4_AVC:
